DTSTART:20260925T105000
DTEND:20260925T115000
SUMMARY:A&amp\;I Convocation with Jeff Ondich
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Skinner Memorial Chapel
DESCRIPTION:Jeff Ondich\, Professor of Computer Science and the Winifred a
 nd Atherton Bean Professor of Science\, Technology\, and Society\, has tau
 ght at Carleton since 1991. He has taught nearly all the required courses 
 in the computer science major\, while focusing mostly on software developm
 ent\, computer security\, and computer systems. He has supervised dozens o
 f teams of computer science majors working on their senior projects ("comp
 s"). He has\, via his students' comps projects and his own research\, coll
 aborated widely across the college\, engaging in projects with people in C
 arleton’s Facilities and Sustainability office\, the New Student Week te
 am\, the sesquicentennial celebration team\, and the departments of Lingui
 stics\, History\, Music\, Cinema and Media Studies\, Studio Art\, and Poli
 tical Science.\n\nMuch of Professor Ondich’s professional work has invol
 ved software design and development. His multi-lingual dictionary applicat
 ions\, published by his company Ultralingua\, Inc.\, have been used by ten
 s of millions of people. In addition\, the software engine that underlies 
 these apps has been incorporated into many programs written by other devel
 opers\, including Augmentative Alternative Communication (AAC) application
 s that help people with speech disabilities to communicate efficiently and
  effectively\; language-learning games and utilities\; an online Dakota-En
 glish dictionary based on modern and historical datasets\; etc.\n\nProfess
 or Ondich has served in a variety of elected and appointed positions at Ca
 rleton\, including Faculty President\, co-chair of the Educational and Cur
 riculum Committee\, and chair of one of the curricular design teams that d
 eveloped the graduation requirements that went into effect in 2010. He ser
 ved as informal co-chair for the computer science half of the Math/CS depa
 rtment for a decade\, and later as chair of the Computer Science Departmen
 t.\n\nProfessor Ondich earned a BA from St. Olaf College and a PhD in from
  the University of Minnesota\, both in mathematics. He is an Offensive Sec
 urity Certified Professional (i.e.\, he knows how to hack into computers).
 \n\nThe title of Professor Ondich presentation is<strong><em> Tech minefie
 lds\, expertise\, and the liberal arts. </em></strong>\n\nThis convocatio
 n is also presented as a virtual webinar. <a href="https://carleton.zoom.
 us/webinar/register/WN_LFV41VEiQr6dIBHsd4u5wg">Please register in advance 
 if you would like to attend via Zoom.</a> After registering\, you will rec
 eive a confirmation email containing information about joining the webinar
 .\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleto
 n.edu/_c/ut8I
ORGANIZER;CN="Convocations":mailto:g8h62604doarbi9ihcipmnhd04@group.calend
 ar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T161649
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f1dn1p0jsoqg1kb5v76hi3lfv4
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260924T034659
DTSTART:20261002T105000
DTEND:20261002T115000
SUMMARY:Convocation with Jonathan Capehart '89 &amp\; H'23
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Skinner Memorial Chapel
DESCRIPTION:<div>\n<div class="gmail_default">\n<p dir="ltr">Jonathan Cape
 hart is a Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist who is co-host of the morning 
 edition of “The Weekend” on MS NOW (7am - 10am) and the New York Times
  bestselling author of <a href="https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/j
 onathan-capehart/yet-here-i-am/9781538767061/" target="_blank" rel="noopen
 er" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.hachett
 ebookgroup.com/titles/jonathan-capehart/yet-here-i-am/9781538767061/&amp\;
 source=gmail&amp\;ust=1787751025904000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2sXVDWjQRttA3J2xVnd_
 nr">“Yet Here I Am: Lessons from A Black Man’s Search for Home.”</a>
  From 2020 until 2025\, he was the anchor of MSNBC’s <a href="https://ww
 w.msnbc.com/capehart" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl=
 "https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.msnbc.com/capehart&amp\;source=g
 mail&amp\;ust=1787751025904000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2sakwMEblfiDLQrZvp7B9f">“T
 he Saturday/Sunday Show with Jonathan Capehart.”</a> At PBS\, Capehart s
 erves as a political analyst on “PBS News Hour” and is featured on the
  popular Friday segment <a href="https://www.pbs.org/newshour/tag/brooks-a
 nd-capehart" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://
 www.google.com/url?q=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/tag/brooks-and-capehart&
 amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1787751025904000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw02Gf_IeenMXO55E
 I7mkDTQ">“Brooks and Capehart.”</a></p>\n<p dir="ltr">Capehart is a <a
  href="https://www.washingtonpost.com/people/jonathan-capehart/" target="_
 blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=h
 ttps://www.washingtonpost.com/people/jonathan-capehart/&amp\;source=gmail&
 amp\;ust=1787751025904000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw07RRRh9BgrgcYx8frdL0HH">former As
 sociate Editor</a> of The Washington Post\, where he served as an opinion 
 writer for 18 years. He was deputy editorial page editor of the New York D
 aily News (2002-2004) and served on its editorial board (1993-2000). His e
 ditorial campaign in 1999 to save the Apollo Theater earned the board the 
 Pulitzer Prize for Editorial Writing. My memoir\, <a href="https://www.gra
 ndcentralpublishing.com/titles/jonathan-capehart/yet-here-i-am/97815387670
 61/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.goog
 le.com/url?q=https://www.grandcentralpublishing.com/titles/jonathan-capeha
 rt/yet-here-i-am/9781538767061/&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=178775102590400
 0&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3BC_OXzuxFZiZ0eUjwLyEG">"Yet Here I Am\,"</a> is a New Yo
 rk Times Best Seller!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\nWhile at Carleton\, Capehart 
 wrote for <em>The</em> <em>Carletonian</em> and hosted a radio show on KR
 LX. He received his BA in political science in 1989. It was with great ple
 asure that Carleton College conferred upon Jonathan Capehart the degree Do
 ctor of Humane Letters\, honoris causa in 2023.\n\nThis convocation is als
 o presented as a virtual webinar. <a href="https://carleton.zoom.us/webin
 ar/register/WN_WKncdqZUTJqcyqmomffX8g">Please register in advance if you w
 ould like to attend via Zoom</a>. After registering\, you will receive a c
 onfirmation email containing information about joining the webinar.\n\n<st
 rong>Seating will be limited at this Convocation due to the nature of this
  event. Doors will open at 10A.M.</strong>\n\nView this event on the Carle
 ton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uujv
ORGANIZER;CN="Convocations":mailto:g8h62604doarbi9ihcipmnhd04@group.calend
 ar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T162025
END:VEVENT
