SUMMARY:Convocation with Valeria Luiselli
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Skinner Memorial Chapel
DESCRIPTION:Valeria Luiselli was born in Mexico City and grew up in South 
 Korea\, South Africa and India. An acclaimed writer of both fiction and no
 nfiction\, she is the author of the essays <a>Tell Me How It Ends and <
 /a><a>Sidewalks</a><a>\; the sonic essay </a><a>Echoes From the Borderlan
 ds\;</a><a> </a>and the novels <a>Faces in the Crowd</a>\, <a>The Story
  of My Teeth</a>\, <a>Lost Children Archive</a><a>\, </a><a>and </a><a>
 Beginning Middle End.</a>\n\nShe is the recipient of a 2019 MacArthur Fell
 owship and the winner of DUBLIN Literary Award\, two Los Angeles Times Boo
 k Prizes\, The Carnegie Medal\, an American Book Award\,  and has been no
 minated for the National Book Critics Circle Award\, the Kirkus Prize\, an
 d the Booker Prize. She has been the recipient of a Bearing Witness Fellow
 ship from the Art for Justice Fund\, a Guggenheim Fellowship and the Vilce
 k Prize. Her work has appeared in The New Yorker\, The New York Times\,
  Granta\, and McSweeney's\, among other publications\, and has been tran
 slated into more than thirty languages. Her ongoing project in sound-scape
 s and oral histories\, Echoes From the Borderlands\, has been featured at
  the <a>DIA Chelsea</a> and the <a>Harvard Art Lab\, among other places
 .</a>\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.car
 leton.edu/_c/ut5r
ORGANIZER;CN="Convocations":mailto:g8h62604doarbi9ihcipmnhd04@group.calend
 ar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T162200
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hmv5qlstuv75jj8cohi2g8ij7c
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260924T034659
DTSTART:20261016T105000
DTEND:20261016T115000
SUMMARY:Family Weekend Convocation with Jack El-Hai '79
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Skinner Memorial Chapel
DESCRIPTION:Jack El-Hai is a journalist who writes nonfiction books\, a
 rticles\, and essays. He covers medicine\, history\, science\, and crime.\
 n\nAmong his published books are The New York Times bestselling The Naz
 i and the Psychiatrist (adapted in 2025 into the movie Nuremberg)\, The 
 Lobotomist\, The Lost Brothers\, and Face in the Mirror. His new book
  The Case of the Autographed Corpse: A Medicine Man and a Mystery Writer 
 in Pursuit of Justice will be published by Pegasus Books in October 2026.
  He has contributed essays and articles to Smithsonian\, The Atlantic\, 
 GQ\, Wired\, Scientific American\, <span style="color: #0a061a\;font-size
 : small">and many other publications. Since 2018\, he has published “Da
 mn History\,” a free monthly newsletter for readers and writers of popul
 ar history.</span>\n\nJack grew up in Los Angeles and is a past presiden
 t of the American Society of Journalists and Authors. He is a two-time w
 inner of the June Roth Award for medical journalism and has won two Minnes
 ota Book Awards. He currently sits on the board of The Loft Literary Cente
 r in Minneapolis. His website is <a href="https://el-hai.com/" target="_b
 lank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=ht
 tps://el-hai.com/&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1786482762721000&amp\;usg=AOv
 Vaw1asd9KIguzxE_d1Cp1uC4O">https://el-hai.com</a>.\n\nHis presentation is 
 titled <em><strong>Writing to Change Hearts and Minds.</strong></em>\n\nTh
 is convocation was also presented as a virtual webinar. <a href="https://
 carleton.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_SthEX-kMSa6tdE7i4e5wuQ">Please regist
 er in advance if you would like to attend via Zoom.</a> After registering
 \, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about join
 ing the webinar.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttp
 s://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut2E
ORGANIZER;CN="Convocations":mailto:g8h62604doarbi9ihcipmnhd04@group.calend
 ar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T162349
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:23t6mcu6g0tfo7msao9fgguk9c
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260924T034659
DTSTART:20261023T105000
DTEND:20261023T115000
SUMMARY:Convocation with Chris Kratt '92
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Skinner Memorial Chapel
DESCRIPTION:Chris Kratt '92 is a writer/director/producer\, wildlife filmm
 aker\, author\, and educator with a degree in biology from Carleton Colleg
 e. Dedicated to introducing people to wild animals and the natural world\,
  Chris reaches audiences through all forms of media. Chris is co-creator a
 nd co-host of several hit television series including <em>WILD KRATTS\, ZO
 BOOMAFOO\,</em> and <em>KRATTS<wbr />’ CREATURES </em>on <em>PBS KIDS</
 em> and <em>BE THE CREATURE</em> on the National Geographic Channel. He 
 has executive produced over 320 episodes of television\, with numerous wri
 ting and directing credits. His projects have garnered such industry and e
 ducational honors as Emmy Award\, Parents’ Choice Award\, Kidscreen\, an
 d Canadian Screen Award.  Chris co-founded the not-for-profit organizatio
 n Kratt Bros. Creature Heroes and is honored to have the newly-discovere
 d Amazonian praying mantis\, Liturgusa krattorum\, named after he and hi
 s brother.\n\nThe title of Chris Kratt '92 presentation is<em> On the Crea
 ture Trail: From the Arb to the Creaturefuge.</em><strong><em>\n</em></str
 ong>\n<p data-path-to-node="2\,0"><strong>There will be no live animals pr
 esent at Convocation. This event will not be recorded or available for fut
 ure viewing.</strong></p>\n<p data-path-to-node="2\,1"><strong>Due to high
  demand\, seating in the main venue will be limited\; doors open at 10:30 
 AM. An overflow viewing location will also be available in Olin Hall 149.<
 /strong></p>\nThis convocation is also presented as a virtual webinar. <a
  href="https://carleton.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_6K2Ki9bGSb2R7fA6i8nruw
 ">Please register in advance if you would like to attend via Zoom</a>. Af
 ter registering\, you will receive a confirmation email containing informa
 tion about joining the webinar.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College
  website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uujq
ORGANIZER;CN="Convocations":mailto:g8h62604doarbi9ihcipmnhd04@group.calend
 ar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T162538
END:VEVENT
